B. The application may include the recommended practices of the Illuminating Engineering Society of North America, a professional engineer, or other authority on outdoor lighting.
(Ord. of 6-8-2015(3), § 1(Exh. A))

743:
A permit shall only be issued subject to the following conditions:
(a) Applicability. The provisions of this section apply to all zoning districts.
(b) Dimensions. All Signs permitted under this section shall be non-illuminated signs no larger than thirty-two (32) square feet and not to exceed a height of eight (8) feet.
(c) LDP and Building Permits. With the issuance of a Land Disturbance Permit (LDP) or building permit by the City of Woodstock, the site or collection of tax parcels subject to the LDP or building permit shall be eligible for one (1) sign per three (3) acres up to a maximum of four (4) Signs. With the expiration of the LDP or building permit, or the issuance of a certificate of occupancy this Sign permit shall also expire.
(d) Occupancy. Property tax parcel or multiple property tax parcels adjacent to each other under common ownership exceeding two (2) acres, or with at least three thousand (3,000) square feet commercial space, are eligible for one (1) Sign subject to the following conditions:
i. Tax parcel(s) are current with property tax payments to the City of Woodstock. Delinquent property tax shall immediately invalidate the permit;
ii. Structures or suites on the property are not occupied, or the property is vacant;
iii. Structures, suites, or tax parcels anticipated to be vacant or unoccupied within the subsequent ninety (90) days may apply for and receive the permit with the completion of a sworn affidavit attesting to the imminent vacancy. Should the premises remain occupied after ninety (90) days, the permit will expire immediately;
iv. With the issuance of certificate of occupancy or occupation tax license and/or with the occupancy of all vacant structures or suites on the tax parcel(s), the permit will expire immediately;
v. Shall require annual renewal concurrent with the due date set on the property tax bill issued by the City of Woodstock. Failure to renew the permit shall immediately invalidate the permit.
(Ord. of 1-11-2016(1))
